    {
      "id": "b9920076c960-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "Which one is the largest among the following?",
      "questionHtml": "Which one is the largest among the following?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "0.725",
          "html": "0.725"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "\\(0.72\\bar5\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(0.72\\bar5\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "\\(0.7\\overline{25}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(0.7\\overline{25}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "\\(0.\\overline{725}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(0.\\overline{725}\\)</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /> <u style=\"font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; display: inline !important;\">Shortcut Trick</u></span>\n<p>To find the largest decimal, expand each up to 4 decimal places:</p>\n<p>A. 0.725 → 0.7250</p>\n<p>B. 0.725 (bar on 5) → 0.7255</p>\n<p>C. 0.7 (bar on 25) → 0.7252</p>\n<p>D. (bar on 725) → 0.7257</p>\n<p>Comparing the 4th decimal place: 7 > 5 > 2 > 0.</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct option is D.</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Alternate Method</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n<p>Option A: 0.725</p>\n<p>Option B: 0.725555...</p>\n<p>Option C: 0.725252...</p>\n<p>Option D: 0.725725...</p>\n<p><strong>Formula Used:</strong></p>\n<p>Comparison of recurring decimals is done by expanding the repeating digits and comparing place by place from left to right.</p>\n<svg width=\"420\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"display:block;margin:12px 0;background:#ffffff;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid #cccccc;\">\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"40\" fill=\"#cc5500\" font-weight=\"bold\">Decimal Digit Comparison</text>\n  <text x=\"40\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#2255cc\">A = 0 . 7 2 5 0 ...</text>\n  <text x=\"40\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#2255cc\">B = 0 . 7 2 5 5 ...</text>\n  <text x=\"40\" y=\"130\" fill=\"#2255cc\">C = 0 . 7 2 5 2 ...</text>\n  <text x=\"40\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#2255cc\">D = 0 . 7 2 5 7 ...</text>\n  <rect x=\"116\" y=\"55\" width=\"15\" height=\"115\" stroke=\"#cc0000\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,3\" />\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#cc0000\" font-size=\"12\">Comparing 4th digit:</text>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"135\" fill=\"#cc0000\" font-weight=\"bold\">7 > 5 > 2 > 0</text>\n</svg>\n<p><strong>Calculations:</strong></p>\n<p>⇒ Expansion of A = 0.725000...</p>\n<p>⇒ Expansion of B = 0.725555...</p>\n<p>⇒ Expansion of C = 0.725252...</p>\n<p>⇒ Expansion of D = 0.725725...</p>\n<p>⇒ Since the first three digits (0.725) are identical for all options, we compare the 4th digit.</p>\n<p>⇒ 4th digit values: A=0, B=5, C=2, D=7.</p>\n<p>⇒ Among these, 7 is the largest value.</p>\n<p>∴ Option D is the largest among the given decimals.</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct option is D.</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Pure Recurring Decimal</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">A decimal in which all the digits after the decimal point repeat. Example: 0.725 (bar on 725) = 725/999.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Mixed Recurring Decimal</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">A decimal in which some digits do not repeat and some digits repeat. Example: 0.725 (bar on 5) = (725 − 72) / 900.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Comparison Rule</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">Always align the decimal points and compare digits from left to right (tenths, hundredths, thousandths, etc.) until a difference is found.</p>",
      "images": [
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png",
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png",
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png"
