    {
      "id": "b9920076c960-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "Among the fractions \\(\\frac{5}{9}\\) , \\(\\frac{11}{18}\\) , \\(\\frac{13}{24}\\) and \\(\\frac{17}{36}\\) , which is the largest?",
      "questionHtml": "Among the fractions&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{5}{9}\\)</span>,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{11}{18}\\)</span>,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{13}{24}\\)</span>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{17}{36}\\)</span>, which is the largest?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{5}{9}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{5}{9}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{13}{24}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{13}{24}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{11}{18}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{11}{18}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{17}{36}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{17}{36}\\)</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Given:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Fractions are:&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{5}{9}, \\frac{11}{18}, \\frac{13}{24}, \\frac{17}{36}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Concept used:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">The smallest fraction is that whose numerator is smallest if the denominator of fractions is equal.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Calculation:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">LCM of 9, 18, 24, 36&nbsp;= 72</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">To compare these fractions,&nbsp;we have to make the denominator of fractions equal to it&#39;s LCM</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{5}{9}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{5}{9}\\)</span>&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{8}{8}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{40}{72}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{11}{18}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{11}{18}\\)</span>&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{4}{4}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{44}{72}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{13}{24}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{13}{24}\\)</span>&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{3}{3}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{39}{72}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{17}{36}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{17}{36}\\)</span>&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{2}{2}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{34}{72}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">So,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{44}{72}\\)</span> has the largest numerator, which is equivalent to&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{11}{18}\\)</span>.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>&there4; The correct answer is&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{11}{18}\\)</span></strong>.</p>\n",
