      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{{12}} + \\frac{1}{{20}} + \\frac{1}{{30}}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; LCM of 6, 12, 20 and 30 = 180</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{{12}} + \\frac{1}{{20}} + \\frac{1}{{30}}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{30+15+9+6}{180}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{30+15+9+6}{180}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{60}{180}=\\frac{1}{3}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Therefore, the simplified value of the fraction is&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)</span></strong>.</p>\n",
